76]. Dots denote genes, coloured by gradients from light to dark by increased strength in either positively (green) or negatively (red) modulating hydrolysate fitness, obtained from screen log2-fold changes. Dot and gene label size denote the multiple-testing adjusted FDRs obtained in the screen. Line thickness indicates confidence of the physical interaction obtained from the STRING database. Network visualization was performed with Gephi [8], using the Force Atlas 2 algorithm for clustering with standard parameters [32].", "funding": "H2020 European Research Council Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft Joachim Herz Stiftung Projekt DEAL", "funding_list": [{"id": 19667023, "title": "H2020 European Research Council Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft Joachim Herz Stiftung Projekt DEAL", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 675592, "created_date": "2021-02-11T04:27:19Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-11T15:11:42Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 47, "name": "CC BY + CC0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["Lignocellulose hydrolysate", "Growth-inhibitor compounds", "CRISPR interference screen", "Yeast fermentation", "Sustainable biotechnology"], "keywords": ["Lignocellulose hydrolysate", "Growth-inhibitor compounds", "CRISPR interference screen", "Yeast fermentation", "Sustainable biotechnology"], "categories": [{"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}], "references": ["https://doi.org/10.1186/1754-6834-3-2", "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biortech.2010.08.037", "https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M403487200", "https://doi.org/10.1023/A%3A1008802704374", "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00505872", "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1176495", "https://doi.org/10.1038/msb4100043", "https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/26.1.73", "https://doi.org/1